---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { LEGAL_UPDATED, SITE, formatDate } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="What Can’t Explain is not: not a newsroom, not a how-to-vote, not a verdict. The hall files the gap between a loud claim and its evidence."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", href: "/" },
    { name: "Disclaimer", href: "/disclaimer" },
  ]}
>
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      We take receipts seriously. That is why it is worth being exact about what a card
      cannot do.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">Updated {formatDate(LEGAL_UPDATED)}.</p>

    <h2 id="not-a-finding">A card is not a verdict</h2>
    <p>
      Filing a claim in the hall is not a finding that the speaker is a fool, or that the
      target is a saint. It means: this accusation arrived at high volume, here is where
      it was said, here is the file we kept, and here is the gap. The caption is an
      eyebrow, not a sentence from a court.
    </p>

    <h2 id="not-ours">The quotes are theirs</h2>
    <p>
      We quote or mark a paraphrase. The words belong to the person who said them, and
      the original page belongs to whoever published it. If the source moves or dies, the
      git file is why we kept a copy — not because we adopted the claim.
    </p>

    <h2 id="not-advice">Not advice, not a how-to-vote</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing here is legal advice, financial advice, or a suggestion about where to put
      a 1. It is not electoral matter asking you to vote for or against anyone. Listing
      a figure, a party, or a journalist is not an endorsement and not a smear of our
      own.
    </p>

    <h2 id="not-complete">Not complete</h2>
    <p>
      Absence from the hall is not a clean bill of health. Presence is not proof the
      speaker is uniquely terrible. We would rather leave a gap than invent a row.
    </p>

    <h2 id="not-the-source">We are not the original outlet</h2>
    <p>
      If we and the original source disagree about what was said, open both. The source
      URL is on the card. If we misquoted, tell us
      <a href={SITE.issues}>here</a> and we will correct the file, not rewrite history
      in place.
    </p>

    <h2 id="independence">Independence</h2>
    <p>
      Published by {SITE.publisher}. Not affiliated with any party, candidate, newsroom,
      or lobby. The same rules apply whichever direction the claim is facing. Longer
      version: <a href="/about">about</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="humour">About the jokes</h2>
    <p>
      The humour is aimed at the missing step, not at a person’s existence. If a caption
      smuggles a second accusation, that is a bug. Email
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
